  "_about": "PACHYCEPHALOSAURUS WYOMINGENSIS (sculpt overlay, 2026-11-05): 4.5 m, ~400 kg, the hips 1.3 m up -- a bipedal ornithischian, the body level over the hips with a broad torso and a deep gut slung between the legs; a short thick S-neck; a 0.55 m skull under a massively thick dome (22 cm of bone), ringed round its back and sides by bony knobs and short blunt spikes on the squamosal shelf, small knobs along the snout; big forward-facing eyes; a short muzzle to a pointed beak with small leaf-shaped teeth behind it; short arms with five small fingers; long strong legs with blunt hoof-like claws; a heavy tail held stiff and level by its ossified tendons. Grey-brown, a paler horn-toned dome, a cream belly. (2026-11-08, review.py: knobs) The squamosal KNOBS are short blunt horns (sides 16) out of the skin along its normal, faired into it -- as field spheres only 1.5 grid cells across they came out as knots of flat facets.",
